Elections
You may choose to add elections to the game. If there is an election, it occurs in the middle of the day - there is discussion both before and after the election. An election is a vote that is handled the same way as the lynch. Whichever player receives the most votes is elected as the role up for election and receives the respective role card (face up). This does not affect their primary role card, or their win condition - they simply gain an additional ability. 
Elected Roles
If you choose to play with several elected roles, only one is elected per day, in the following order: Mayor, Reporter, Guardian. If a player with an elected role dies, it can be decided before the game starts whether the role is immediately passed to a successor once or put up for election again.
The following rule variants are recommended: No Elections with Flips (Basic); Mayor with Flips (Intermediate); Mayor, Reporter, and Guardian with No Flips (Advanced).
